# Egress relay for proxy-only mode -- TEMPLATE, NOT A USABLE CONFIG.
#
# Listens on the internal harvest-egress network, where the worker has no route of its own,
# and forwards everything to the upstream ISP proxy. The worker cannot reach the internet
# except through this process, so "proxy-only" is a property of the Docker routing, not of a
# firewall rule somebody has to remember to load.
#
# THE `Upstream` LINE IS NOT HERE ON PURPOSE. It carries a username and password, so it must
# never live in a tracked file. entrypoint.sh appends it at container start, reading the
# credential from a 0600 untracked file bind-mounted at /run/secrets/egress-upstream and
# writing the assembled config to a tmpfs. See "Upstream proxy credential" in DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# This file is mounted at /etc/tinyproxy/tinyproxy.conf.template, NOT at tinyproxy's default
# config path, and that rename matters: with no `Upstream` line tinyproxy still runs happily
# and connects to destinations DIRECTLY from this VPS's own address, which silently defeats
# proxy-only egress while every other check still passes. Mounting this file as the real
# config would produce exactly that. entrypoint.sh instead refuses to start when the
# credential is absent, so the failure is loud rather than a quiet attribution leak.
User nobody
Group nogroup
Port 8888
Timeout 600
# Only the internal network can reach this; it is not published anywhere.
Allow 0.0.0.0/0
ConnectPort 443
ConnectPort 80
# Info does not log request URLs or the upstream credential. Raising this to Connect logs
# every destination, and LogLevel Debug can echo header material -- neither is wanted on a
# host whose whole point is reducing what is attributable to it.
LogLevel Info
DisableViaHeader Yes
